                <pb facs="0624" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg526"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Jackson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic">September 11,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1105.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 1368, of the 23d ultimo, stating that American soldiers and sailors
                    will always be able to avail themselves of the arrangements made for the sick
                    and wounded by the German Trained Nurse Association, and you are instructed to
                    express in proper quarter this Government’s cordial appreciation of the
                    arrangement in question.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
